## Findings
1. advisory — brief:40 The phone phase strip shows `aria-current` to assistive technology only. The prototype adds no style for `.board__strip-item[aria-current="true"]`, so on the 390 captures every phase button looks the same. A sighted phone user still cannot see which phase is in view, which is the problem Intent (brief:15) names. This line was written by an agent, not ruled by the Patron. Default 2 (brief:121) offers the Patron "machine-readable" only and does not ask them about a visible cue. Replacement for brief:40: "`PhaseNavigation` remains a presentation child of `BoardView`. It observes `.board__columns`, computes the column whose left edge is nearest the track's left edge, and places `aria-current=\"true\"` on that phase button, which w025.css draws with an ink border and `--rule` fill and no accent colour (DIRECTION §3: an accent never marks a state). Its tap still calls the existing `scrollColumnIntoView`; its own horizontal offset changes only enough to keep the current phase name visible. It creates no second lifecycle state and no route state." Also add "and visible" after "machine-readable" in Default 2. [severity: S4] [class: ui×sense-on-screen] — check: none: a W-411-b2 served assertion that the `aria-current` strip button's computed border or background differs from its siblings
2. advisory — brief:25 The selected lifecycle card gets `background: var(--wash)`. Every waiting card (`.board__card--amber`) already has that background. Opening from the waiting strip always selects a waiting card, so after close the "selected background" (brief:86) looks no different on that card. On a non-waiting card, selection looks like a waiting card without its amber rule. b4 checks only that a CSS rule exists, and its served fixture card W-5 is a waiting card, so nothing tests whether the change is visible. Replacement for brief:25: "`apps/web/src/components/w025.css`: remove the dead reason style, keep the detail header and Close control sticky, and give selected lifecycle cards a background distinct from both `--surface` and the waiting `--wash` (the Inbox's selected `--rule` fill, held to the W-341 contrast test), with DIRECTION's 120ms background transition and reduced-motion zeroing." In brief:86, after "selected background", add "that differs from the same card's unselected background". [severity: S2] [class: ui×sense-on-screen] — check: none: a W-411-b4 served assertion that W-5's computed background-color differs before and after it is selected

